 "text": "A hacked AI coding tool just ran up bills of over a thousand dollars on people's AI accounts. Here's what happened. Attackers broke into OpenCode's web platform where users had saved their AI keys and spent on those keys. Open AI, Anthropic, and Google accounts, with spend alerts going off overnight. If you've ever pasted a key into an AI tool, check three settings today. First, a spending limit. Set a monthly cap wherever your account allows it. Second, separate keys. One key per tool so one leak doesn't open everything. Third, who can use them? Delete old keys and remove people who've left. It takes five minutes and it beats a surprise bill. Want my AI starter pack? Comment AI and I'll send it to you free."
